\par\par \uc2 The Americas\par \uc2 Opinion\par \b \uc2 Biden's Troubling Latin Agenda; Funding for political activism and  \highlight22\uc2 abortion \highlight\uc2  won't create jobs in the region.\b0\par\par\uc2 By Mary Anastasia O'Grady \par \uc2 832 \uc2 words\par \uc2 7 February 2021\par 21:16 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 When developed countries support equality before the law and property rights in poor countries, the left labels them imperialists. But use U.S. taxpayers' resources to promote the termination of unborn life in poor countries, and progressives call it "health" spending. A similar language game is played when international socialists organize political factions under the banner of "democracy" to consolidate power.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and democratic socialism are two causes the Biden administration plans to champion in the Northern Triangle of Central America\u8212\'20\'14Honduras, Guatemala and El Salvador. Sovereignty, respect for local cultural norms, and the economic aspirations of millions of have-nots have never been high ideals in Washington. But now the condescending ideologues are resupplied. The problem is likely to get worse.\par \par \uc2 Latin Americans have reason to distrust President Biden, who had special responsibility for the region during the Obama administration. One notable disaster in that time was Colombia's surrender to the narco-trafficking group FARC. The agreement was cooked up in Havana with U.S. help. Colombians rejected it in a referendum, but then-President \uc2 Juan Manuel Santos\uc2  pushed it through anyway, with backing from Team Obama.\par \par \uc2 FARC leaders got amnesty and unelected seats in Congress, but the agreement has been a disaster for the South American nation. The cocaine business has exploded anew, FARC honchos have been caught in drug deals, and coca-growing regions are again immersed in bloody conflict. The discredited Mr. Santos has been reduced to lobbying the U.S. to take Havana off its list of state sponsors of terrorism.\par \par \uc2 In Central America, Biden administration foreign-policy makers want to reproduce a version of the United Nations' International Commission Against Impunity in Guatemala (a k a CIGIG) that would span all three countries in the Northern Triangle.\par \par \uc2 Helping countries develop independent, transparent and accountable institutions is a worthy foreign-policy goal. But CICIG was none of that.\par \par \uc2 The commission prosecuted some criminals. But without checks, Commissioner \uc2 Iv\u225\'00\'E1n Vel\u225\'00\'E1squez\uc2  gained absolute power and used it to unleash a reign of terror against Guatemalan society. What was billed as a way to help the country fight organized crime and build a credible judicial system was weaponized by the left. \uc2 James Comey\uc2 's \uc2 FBI\uc2  going after Trump supporters had nothing on Mr. Vel\u225\'00\'E1squez. The most corrupt entrepreneurs and politicians stayed out of jail by cheering his misdeeds.\par \par \uc2 CICIG abuses gained international attention when lawyers for the Russian migrant family of Igor Bitkov, whom it targeted, {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.csce.gov/sites/helsinkicommission.house.gov/files/unofficial-transcript/Bitkov hearing transcript - Unofficial.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 testified}}}\uc2  at a \uc2 Helsinki Commission\uc2  hearing in Washington in 2018. They told of the gross mistreatment of the family, allegedly at the behest of \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden, who claimed to be an expert on CICIG, never condemned the collapse of due process or the cruelty the commission used to force confessions. He never even spoke up for the Bitkovs, whose 3-year-old son was thrown into an orphanage when they were jailed.\par \par \uc2 Guatemalans deserve an accounting. Instead Biden stenographers in the media are busy sanitizing his role in the CICIG story. The Bitkov family, still stuck in the corrupt Guatemalan legal system, remains a symbol of the dearth of empathy inside the Beltway.\par \par \uc2 But Joe cares deeply about the region\u8212\'20\'14or so we are told. He will prove it now by pumping $4 billion into a variety of Northern Triangle social and activist political organizations. It won't generate jobs beyond the aid industry.\par \par \uc2 An equally important agenda item for Mr. Biden is the export of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the developing world. To that end, on his eighth day in office he signed an executive decree to allow U.S. taxpayer dollars to fund \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  providers operating overseas. This from the guy who pledges dignity for poor nations.\par \par \uc2 Plenty of Americans object. In a January Marist {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.toomey.senate.gov/imo/media/doc/2021 Marist Poll[3].pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 poll}}}\uc2  77% of respondents said they oppose U.S. financing to "support \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  in other countries," well above the 53% who said they are pro-life.\par \par \uc2 Some of these Americans may have an innate sense of respect for other cultures. In the developing world there is a strong belief that \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't only take a life but that taking away the rights of the unborn undermines the ethical foundations of society.\par \par \uc2 This creed is captured in a recent "Culture of Life Africa" {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zymBhgUqoh4&feature=youtu.be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 video.}}}\uc2  The 16-minute production features people across the continent pleading with Mr. Biden not to bring \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  to their shores. Honduras recently passed a constitutional amendment (requiring four-fifths approval in two different legislative sessions) prohibiting \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 In Honduras and many other poor countries where \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains illegal, organizations like \uc2 International Planned Parenthood\uc2  can now use \uc2 U.S. government\uc2  funds to promote their industry. Mr. Biden doesn't need to share the moral convictions of pro-life nations. But his contempt for their views is troubling.\par \par \uc2 Write to O'Grady@wsj.com.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/bidens-troubling-latin-agenda-11612732559"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Biden's Troubling Latin Agenda}}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210207eh27002mh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
