\par\par \uc2 Europe News\par \uc2 World\par \b \uc2 As Poland  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Law Takes Effect, Women Protest; More demonstrations are planned after restrictions on terminating pregnancy grow tighter\b0\par\par\uc2 By Natalia Ojewska \par \uc2 439 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2021\par 16:46 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WARSAW\u8212\'20\'14Thousands of women took to the streets of Polish cities after an extensive ban on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  took effect, three months after {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/polands-top-court-tightens-strict-abortion-laws-11603397449"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a court ruled that it was unconstitutional  }}}\uc2  to terminate pregnancies because of fetal abnormalities.\par \par \uc2 A rights group called Women's Strike led crowds of people into the streets of Warsaw, Krakow and other cities as the law took effect at midnight, after it was upheld by Poland's Constitutional Tribunal. The ruling, more than 200 pages long, said that allowing \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  because of congenital defects violated the Polish constitution, which protects all human life.\par \par \uc2 Further protests are planned this week, reflecting broader concern among younger Poles over the conservative policies of Poland's government, which is allied with the Catholic Church and has tried to tighten Poland's already-strict \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws since coming to power in 2015. {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/poland-abortion-ruling-sparks-one-of-countrys-largest-protests-in-years-11604090139"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Similar protests last fall  }}}\uc2  drew tens of thousands of people in Warsaw alone.\par \par \uc2 Many demonstrators say they are concerned over the way {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/polands-ruling-nationalists-eye-new-term-as-voting-begins-11570953095"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 the ruling Law and Justice party  }}}\uc2  previously {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/polands-ruling-party-moves-to-impose-its-will-on-supreme-court-1512763287"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 purged members of the Constitutional Tribunal  }}}\uc2  and replaced them with conservative judges, drawing criticism from the \uc2 European Union\uc2  and elsewhere.\par \par \uc2 Anita Czerwi\u324\'01\'44ska, spokeswoman for the Law and Justice party, said it is still studying the court's judgment before commenting. The party has said that the court is responsive to the wishes of Polish voters, who have repeatedly handed Law and Justice majorities in Poland's parliament.\par \par \uc2 Marta Lempart, leader of the Women's Strike group, said late Wednesday that the new restrictions on \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  were an attack on the freedoms of all Poles.\par \par \uc2 "This is the fight for freedom, for me, for my daughters and for all women, that motivated me to come here," said a protester, Joanna Warchulska, 43 years old. "I think that there are certain things that demand that we get up from our sofas and to take to the streets."\par \par \uc2 Poland already had some of the most restrictive \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  laws in Europe, allowing it in only a few cases, including when doctors found evidence of congenital abnormalities or other damage in fetuses.\par \par \uc2 Before the coronavirus pandemic, around 150,000 Poles traveled abroad each year to terminate pregnancies. Fewer than 2,000 legal abortions take place in Poland each year, experts say, with 98% of them performed because of abnormalities detected in the fetus.\par \par \uc2 The new law only allows abortions in cases of rape, incest or when the health of the women is at stake.\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/as-poland-abortion-law-takes-effect-women-protest-11611852378"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 As Poland \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Law Takes Effect, Women Protest  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210128eh1s005eh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
