\par\par \uc2 Politics and Policy\par \uc2 Politics\par \b \uc2 Biden Targets  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Restrictions as Fight Looms in Congress; President ends policy that prohibits federal funds from going to foreign-aid groups that perform abortions or provide related services\b0\par\par\uc2 By Catherine Lucey and Kristina Peterson \par \uc2 1,099 \uc2 words\par \uc2 28 January 2021\par 19:54 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14President Biden ended a policy that prohibits federal funds from going to foreign-aid groups that perform abortions or provide related services, one of several moves likely to spark renewed debate over \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden can make some of his intended changes quickly, but others will likely run into hurdles in Congress, where Democrats hold narrow majorities. Echoing many Democrats and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates, he has said he backs ending a provision in spending bills known as the Hyde Amendment, which bars federal funds from being used for abortions except in limited cases.\par \par \uc2 Many Republicans say they will oppose any spending bill that doesn't include the amendment.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden on Thursday issued a "presidential memorandum to protect and expand access to comprehensive \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care," as part of a series of health-care-related actions. Among its effects will be to reverse a rule known as the "Mexico City policy"\u8212\'20\'14or, to critics, the "global gag rule."\par \par \uc2 SHARE YOUR THOUGHTS\par \par \uc2 How do you think Biden will approach \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  as president? Join the conversation below.\par \par \uc2 The policy bars foreign nongovernmental groups that get U.S. funding from providing abortions or \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  information. Recent Democratic administrations have ended the policy, and Republican administrations have reinstated it.\par \par \uc2 The memorandum will also direct the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2  to review a Trump administration rule that {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-curbs-federal-funding-for-clinics-providing-abortions-11550866834"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 cut off federal funding for family-planning organizations }}}\uc2  such as \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2 . Any change would have to go through a regulatory process. A White House official said Thursday that the final decision will be at the discretion of the agency.\par \par \uc2 In the Oval Office on Thursday Mr. Biden described the health-care actions as an effort to "undo the damage [former President Donald] Trump has done."\par \par \uc2 "It is a good down payment, absolutely," Ilyse Hogue, president of Naral Pro-Choice America, said of Mr. Biden's anticipated early moves, adding that advocates of wider \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access know the hurdles facing a repeal of the Hyde Amendment.\par \par \uc2 "We're not blind to the fact that we're going to have some recalcitrant individuals in both chambers on our hands," she said. "We think we have the polling, we think we have the movement, we think we have the energy."\par \par \uc2 Polls show {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/record-71-of-voters-oppose-overturning-roe-v-wade-1532379600"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 most Americans say \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  should be legal }}}\uc2 , but support is much higher among Democrats than Republicans. Overall support has grown in recent years.\par \par \uc2 Democrats assumed control in Washington after years of conservative efforts to challenge federal law allowing abortions. A number of Republican-led states have pushed limits or effective bans, while some Democratic-led states have sought to loosen restrictions.\par \par \uc2 Antiabortion groups criticized Mr. Biden's early moves.\par \par \uc2 "This is a clear payback to the \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  lobby, which heavily supported the Biden-Harris ticket during the campaign," said Mallory Quigley, spokeswoman for the antiabortion group Susan B. Anthony List. "And it's a cold shoulder to millions of Americans across the political spectrum who are opposed to taxpayer funding of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  and \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  businesses."\par \par \uc2 The 1976 Hyde Amendment bars federal funding for \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  with exceptions for victims of rape or incest or if the mother's life is in danger. \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  opponents say it ensures tax dollars don't go to paying for the procedure.\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates say it disproportionately affects low-income women who are Medicaid recipients because the program doesn't pay for abortions with federal funds except in limited circumstances.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Biden supported the Hyde Amendment for years before {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/biden-reverses-stance-on-hyde-amendment-citing-roe-v-wade-11559871101"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 reversing his position during his presidential campaign }}}\uc2 , under pressure from Democrats and advocates. He cited Republican efforts to limit access to abortions and overturn the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision.\par \par \uc2 While many Democrats have opposed the amendment, they have found it difficult to remove it from spending bills. The party currently has {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/smaller-house-majority-poses-headaches-for-democrats-11605132137"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 a razor-thin 221-211 hold on the House }}}\uc2 , where spending bills can pass with a simple majority. But in the Senate, split 50-50, most legislation must win 60 votes, and most Republicans oppose \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  access.\par \par \uc2 Democrats hold the Senate majority because Vice President \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  has the tiebreaking vote, and efforts have reignited among \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights advocates to make dismantling the Hyde Amendment a priority. But Senate Democrats don't appear to have enough support to lower that 60-vote threshold, making it unlikely they could eliminate the amendment now.\par \par \uc2 A group of 200 House Republicans said in a letter to congressional leaders this week that they will oppose any spending bills that strip out or weaken the Hyde provision.\par \par \uc2 "At the outset of the Congress, it's the right time to draw a line in the sand and say for the 200 of us who signed the letter, we will not vote for any spending measures that don't provide Hyde protections," said Republican Study Committee Chairman Jim Banks (R., Ind.), who organized the letter.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, new \uc2 House Appropriations Committee\uc2  Chairwoman Rosa DeLauro (D., Conn.) has said she won't include the amendment in House spending bills, calling it "one of the biggest barriers to low-income women's access to health care."\par \par \uc2 Rep. \uc2 David Price\uc2  (D., N.C.), a senior member of the \uc2 House Appropriations Committee\uc2 , said removing the provision would be a challenge, but "I think we've got to try."\par \par \uc2 Democrats are now mostly opposed to the Hyde Amendment, and the party's 2016 platform called for the repeal of the amendment for the first time. But for decades, Democrats have included the amendment in legislation that required bipartisan support. In 2019, Democratic Sens. Joe Manchin of West Virginia and Bob Casey of Pennsylvania voted in support of a permanent ban on federal funding for most abortions.\par \par \uc2 A group of 47 Senate Republicans reintroduced legislation on Thursday that would make the Hyde amendment permanent.\par \par \uc2 A coalition of \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 -rights groups have outlined demands for this administration, including a review of a Food and Drug Administration requirement that women make {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-restores-mandate-that-women-pick-up-abortion-drugs-in-person-11610500527"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 in-person visits to pick up prescriptions for \b  \highlight22abortion\b0 \highlight22  drugs }}}\uc2 , even during the coronavirus pandemic.\par \par \uc2 Planned Parenthood Federation of America\uc2  President \uc2 Alexis McGill Johnson\uc2  said the coalition intends "to hold \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 , \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  and this administration to the highest standard and ensure that they enact policy that advances sexual- and \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive-health\b0 \highlight\uc2  access."\par \par \uc2 Write to Catherine Lucey at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:catherine.lucey@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 catherine.lucey@wsj.com }}}\uc2  and Kristina Peterson at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:kristina.peterson@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 kristina.peterson@wsj.com }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210128eh1s002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw254\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3810\pichgoal600
