\par\par \uc2 U.S. News\par \uc2 US\par \b \uc2 Supreme Court Restores Mandate That Women Pick Up  \highlight22\uc2 Abortion \highlight\uc2  Drugs in Person; Lower court had suspended requirement due to coronavirus hazards\b0\par\par\uc2 By Jess Bravin \par \uc2 733 \uc2 words\par \uc2 13 January 2021\par 02:24 GMT\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal Online\par \uc2 WSJO\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 WASHINGTON\u8212\'20\'14The Supreme Court Tuesday reinstated requirements that women seeking medication abortions make in-person visits to pick up their prescriptions, siding with the Trump administration over medical organizations that argued the mandate exposes patients to needless risks during the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/livecoverage/latest-updates/covid"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 coronavirus pandemic }}}\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The court's three liberal justices dissented from the majority's brief, unsigned order.\par \par \uc2 In March, the \uc2 Food and Drug Administration\uc2  relaxed in-person dispensing requirements for other drugs and encouraged telemedicine to reduce the spread of Covid-19. But the Trump administration, which opposes \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights, left in place regulations requiring women to make in-person visits to a hospital, clinic or physician's office to pick up mifepristone, one of two drugs used to induce a medication \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists\uc2 , an organization of women's health-care physicians, and other groups sued the \uc2 FDA\uc2  over its exclusion of mifepristone, also known by the brand name Mifeprex.\par \par \uc2 The group's president, Dr. Eva Chalas, said patients should be able to obtain mifepristone, like other drugs, through mail delivery.\par \par \uc2 "We are deeply disappointed that our members and their patients will now be faced with an unnecessary increase in risk of exposure to Covid-19 as the virus rages across the country. Access to \b \highlight22\uc2 reproductive health\b0 \highlight\uc2  care should not come with a caveat," Dr. Chalas said.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  Case\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/scotus_dissent_jan_12_2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Read the Dissent }}}\uc2  (Jan. 12)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-puts-off-decision-on-reinstating-abortion-pill-restrictions-11602208067"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Puts Off Decision on Reinstating \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Pill Restrictions }}}\uc2  (Oct. 8)\par \par \uc2 * {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-asks-high-court-to-reinstate-mandate-that-women-obtain-abortion-pill-in-person-11598481735"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Trump Administration Asks High Court to Reinstate Mandate That Women Obtain \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Pill In-Person }}}\uc2  (Aug. 26)\par \par \uc2 In July, U.S. District Judge Theodore Chuang in Greenbelt, Md., suspended the in-person pickup rule, finding that it imposed a "substantial obstacle in the path of women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." The Fourth U.S. Circuit Court of Appeals, in Richmond, Va., denied the government's appeal.\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/trump-administration-asks-high-court-to-reinstate-mandate-that-women-obtain-abortion-pill-in-person-11598481735"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 appealed to the Supreme Court in August }}}\uc2 , prompting the justices to {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-puts-off-decision-on-reinstating-abortion-pill-restrictions-11602208067"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 return the issue for reconsideration to the lower court }}}\uc2 , while leaving the stay intact.\par \par \uc2 Over that time, the court's composition shifted significantly, with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/ruth-bader-ginsburg-dies-11600472623"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 death in September }}}\uc2  of the liberal Justice \uc2 Ruth Bader Ginsburg\uc2  allowing Mr. Trump and Senate Republicans to cement the conservative majority with the {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/amy-coney-barrett-set-to-be-confirmed-as-supreme-court-justice-11603721947"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 confirmation }}}\uc2  of Justice Amy Coney Barrett.\par \par \uc2 Tuesday's majority published no explanation for its decision, but Chief Justice \uc2 John Roberts\uc2  issued a brief statement saying his vote to reinstate the regulation followed his view that government officials rather than courts should determine public-health measures.\par \par \uc2 "My view is that courts owe significant deference to the politically accountable entities" with the necessary "background, competence and expertise" to make public-health determinations, the chief justice wrote.\par \par \uc2 Dissenting, Justice \uc2 Sonia Sotomayor\uc2  wrote that the policy "imposes an unnecessary, unjustifiable, irrational, and undue burden on women seeking an \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://s.wsj.net/public/resources/documents/scotus_dissent_jan_12_2021.pdf"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Justice Sotomayor's dissent }}}\uc2 , joined by Justice Elena Kagan, argued that the Trump administration's position made no sense.\par \par \uc2 Most women seeking abortions within the first 10 weeks of pregnancy use medication abortions, Justice Sotomayor wrote. They can receive medical counseling via remote consultations and administer the drugs themselves at home. Mifepristone is the only one of 20,000 drugs that is subject to an FDA-imposed in-person pickup requirement.\par \par \uc2 "Government policy now permits patients to receive prescriptions for powerful opioids without leaving home, yet still requires women to travel to a doctor's office to pick up mifepristone, only to turn around, go home, and ingest it without supervision," Justice Sotomayor wrote.\par \par \uc2 She took particular aim at the Trump administration's argument that women who were unable to obtain mifepristone within the initial weeks of pregnancy "can still seek out a surgical \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Justice Sotomayor wrote. "What a callous response."\par \par \uc2 The Trump administration also opposes surgical abortions, and in other cases has weighed in with support for state laws restricting the procedure.\par \par \uc2 Justice \uc2 Stephen Breyer\uc2  also voted against reinstating the in-person pickup rule, but didn't issue or join an opinion.\par \par \uc2 The rule likely will be reviewed in the coming weeks, as President-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  supports \b \highlight22\uc2 abortion\b0 \highlight\uc2  rights and has called for recognizing them through a federal statute.\par \par \uc2 Write to Jess Bravin at {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "mailto:jess.bravin@wsj.com"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 jess.bravin@wsj.com }}}\par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://www.wsj.com/articles/supreme-court-restores-mandate-that-women-pick-up-abortion-drugs-in-person-11610500527"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 Supreme Court Restores Mandate That Women Pick Up \b  \highlight22Abortion\b0 \highlight22  Drugs in Person  }}}\par \par \uc2 Document WSJO000020210113eh1d000b5\par }\par \b \uc2 Search Summary\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9360\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 r